Task: Implement (Green) - PUT /orders/{id} full-replace endpoint

Summary:
Added a tapir PUT /orders/{id} endpoint (replaceOrderEndpoint), same shape as
PATCH's (UpdateOrderRequest body: quantity, status; 200 + OrderResponse; 404
via notFoundOutput for an unknown id). Both PATCH and PUT delegate to
OrderStore.update - there's no behavioral difference between them at the
store layer, since this resource has no other client-writable fields; PUT
exists purely so clients get REST-conventional idempotent-full-replace
semantics as a distinct verb from PATCH's partial-update semantics, per the
user's explicit request.

Refactored: extracted the PATCH handler's store-call/logging block into a
shared updateLogic(store, logger, httpMethod)(id, req) helper, parameterized
only by the logged HTTP method string ("PATCH" vs "PUT") - avoids duplicating
the whole block for what is otherwise identical logic.

Files changed:
- src/main/scala/orderservice/{Main,OrderRoutes}.scala

Why: Implements this track's Phase 7 scope addition (spec.md FR4 update,
2026-09-29) - completes the CRUD surface to five endpoints.

